Deployed to the edge PBX on 2026-08-29. Applies on top of 2d0837f (the wedge/crash
backport in chan-quectel-wedge-crash-fix.patch), against the RoEdAl fork.

WHY
  chan_quectel's idle keepalive is a bare "AT" (PING_AT, chosen because query_time is
  unset and defaults to 0), declared with ATQ_CMD_TIMEOUT_SHORT = 1 second while every
  other command gets MEDIUM (5s) or LONG (40s). The deadline is stamped after the write
  in at_queue.c, so it is a true 1s modem-response budget, not queue-wait.

  A timeout on CMD_AT is listed under "critical errors" in at_response_error(), which
  does `goto e_return` -> returns -1 -> cmd_timeout() logs "Fail to handle response" and
  sets terminate_monitor = 1. The device is torn down and restarted with no retry: one
  missed heartbeat kills the modem.

  Observed on shop5 on 2026-08-29. A test SMS went out on a SIM with 0 kr credit; the
  submit stalled (Asterisk logged "[shop5][SMSTEXT] Error sending message"), the modem
  could not answer a bare AT inside 1s, and the device restart-looped every 15s for 90s
  before recovering. 12 such timeouts on shop5 that day; zero on shop1/shop2 across the
  preceding six days of log.

FIX
  Give the keepalive MEDIUM (5s). A genuinely wedged modem is still detected, four
  seconds later. Nothing else changes.

NOTE
  The edge build tree also carries an unrelated uncommitted change to src/mutils.h
  (enum2str_def uses a plain ternary instead of the S_COR macro). That predates this work
  and is part of what builds the currently-deployed module; it is not included here.

Rollback: /home/phone/chan_quectel.so.rollback-20260829-1323 (md5 dc18aba12bab),
then `sudo systemctl restart asterisk`. Module deployed by this patch: md5 3e507974a2f0.

diff --git a/src/at_command.c b/src/at_command.c
index 8b6f763..0bb8d0a 100644
--- a/src/at_command.c
+++ b/src/at_command.c
@@ -121,7 +121,13 @@ static int __attribute__((format(printf, 4, 5))) at_enqueue_generic(struct cpvt*
 
 int at_enqueue_at(struct cpvt* cpvt)
 {
-    static const at_queue_cmd_t cmd = ATQ_CMD_DECLARE_STFT(CMD_AT, RES_OK, AT_CMD(at), 0, ATQ_CMD_TIMEOUT_SHORT, 0);
+    /* MEDIUM (5s), not SHORT (1s). This is the idle keepalive, and a timeout on CMD_AT is
+     * classified as a CRITICAL error in at_response_error() -- it tears the device down and
+     * restarts it with no retry. A modem busy with SMS PDU I/O, or stalled on a submit the
+     * network will not accept (an out-of-credit SIM), routinely needs more than 1s to answer a
+     * bare AT, so the 1s budget turned ordinary backpressure into a 15s restart loop. 5s still
+     * detects a genuinely wedged modem, just four seconds later. */
+    static const at_queue_cmd_t cmd = ATQ_CMD_DECLARE_STFT(CMD_AT, RES_OK, AT_CMD(at), 0, ATQ_CMD_TIMEOUT_MEDIUM, 0);
 
     if (at_queue_insert_const(cpvt, &cmd, 1u, 1)) {
         chan_quectel_err = E_QUEUE;
